      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to simplify the given equation. The equation is:\n\n\\[5 = \\frac{x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x}{x + 2}\\]\n\nWe start by performing polynomial long division on the numerator \\(x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x\\) by the denominator \\(x + 2\\).\n\n1. Divide the leading term of the numerator \\(x^3\\) by the leading term of the denominator \\(x\\) to get \\(x^2\\).\n2. Multiply \\(x^2\\) by \\(x + 2\\) to get \\(x^3 + 2x^2\\).\n3. Subtract \\(x^3 + 2x^2\\) from \\(x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x\\) to get \\(-4x^2 - 8x\\).\n4. Divide the leading term \\(-4x^2\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(-4x\\).\n5. Multiply \\(-4x\\) by \\(x + 2\\) to get \\(-4x^2 - 8x\\).\n6. Subtract \\(-4x^2 - 8x\\) from \\(-4x^2 - 8x\\) to get \\(0\\).\n\nSo, the division gives us:\n\n\\[x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x = (x + 2)(x^2 - 4x)\\]\n\nThus, the equation simplifies to:\n\n\\[5 = \\frac{(x + 2)(x^2 - 4x)}{x + 2}\\]\n\nFor \\(x \\neq -2\\), we can cancel \\(x + 2\\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[5 = x^2 - 4x\\]\n\nRearrange this equation to form a standard quadratic equation:\n\n\\[x^2 - 4x - 5 = 0\\]\n\nNext, we factor the quadratic equation:\n\n\\[x^2 - 4x - 5 = (x - 5)(x + 1) = 0\\]\n\nSo, the solutions are:\n\n\\[x = 5 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -1\\]\n\nThe sum of the \\(x\\)-values that satisfy the equation is:\n\n\\[5 + (-1) = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{4}\\]",
